{"title":"Career Roadmap · Legal Aid Counsel","role":"Legal Aid Counsel","summary":"A Legal Aid Counsel provides legal representation and assistance to people who cannot reasonably afford private legal services or who are otherwise entitled to legal aid under applicable law and legal-aid schemes.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Criminal Law"},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"flow","items":["Legal Issue","Applicable Law","Arguments","Court's Reasoning","Decision"]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Legal Aid Counsel provides legal representation and assistance to people who cannot reasonably afford private legal services or who are otherwise entitled to legal aid under applicable law and legal-aid schemes."},{"type":"p","text":"In India, legal-aid work can involve institutions and mechanisms associated with the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA), State Legal Services Authorities, District Legal Services Authorities, legal-aid clinics, courts, prisons, NGOs, and other approved organizations."},{"type":"p","text":"A Legal Aid Counsel may assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal defence"},{"text":"Bail matters"},{"text":"Remand-related proceedings"},{"text":"Legal consultation"},{"text":"Representation before courts"},{"text":"Victim-support matters"},{"text":"Prisoner legal assistance"},{"text":"Legal awareness"},{"text":"Documentation and applications"},{"text":"Appeals and related proceedings"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact appointment route, eligibility and remuneration depend on the relevant legal-services authority, panel and current rules."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated LLB","Criminal Law Internships","Moot Courts + Legal Aid Clinic","Advocate Qualification / Enrolment","Court Practice / Legal Aid Experience","Legal Aid Panel / Legal Aid Counsel","Experienced Legal Aid Counsel","Senior Counsel / Legal Services Professional","Legal Aid / Access-to-Justice Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"A student should understand that an LLB by itself does not make someone an advocate entitled to practise in court. For court practice in India, the applicable enrolment and professional requirements must be fulfilled."}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During Integrated LLB","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Core Knowledge"],"rows":[[{"text":"Criminal Law"},{"text":"Offences, liability and defences"}],[{"text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"text":"Investigation, arrest, bail, trial procedure"}],[{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Admissibility, relevance and proof"}],[{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Fundamental rights and due process"}],[{"text":"Human Rights"},{"text":"Rights of accused, victims and vulnerable persons"}],[{"text":"Legal Aid"},{"text":"Access to justice and legal-services framework"}],[{"text":"Advocacy"},{"text":"Oral submissions and court procedure"}],[{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Statutes, judgments and precedents"}],[{"text":"Drafting"},{"text":"Applications, petitions and legal documents"}],[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Professional conduct and confidentiality"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For current criminal-law study, students should learn the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), and Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA) and the latest amendments and judicial interpretation applicable at the time of practice."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Legal Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal reasoning"},{"text":"Constitutional principles"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Legal writing"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Case analysis"},{"text":"Basic criminal-law concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start reading judgments rather than relying exclusively on textbook summaries."},{"type":"h","text":"Build the habit:"}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Criminal Law Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Substantive criminal law"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Constitutional protections"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Police and investigation processes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrest"},{"text":"Bail"},{"text":"Remand"},{"text":"Search and seizure"},{"text":"Investigation"},{"text":"Charge"},{"text":"Trial"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Revision"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Criminal Advocacy"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bail applications"},{"text":"Anticipatory-bail concepts where applicable"},{"text":"Remand proceedings"},{"text":"Criminal complaints"},{"text":"Charge-related proceedings"},{"text":"Evidence examination"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Final arguments"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Criminal revisions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Participate in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Moot courts"},{"text":"Trial advocacy competitions"},{"text":"Legal-aid clinics"},{"text":"Client counselling"},{"text":"Mock trials"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Years — Access to Justice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"District courts"},{"text":"Magistrate courts"},{"text":"Sessions courts"},{"text":"Legal Services Authorities"},{"text":"Prison legal-aid programs"},{"text":"Legal-aid clinics"},{"text":"Human-rights organizations"},{"text":"Criminal-law chambers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to work with clients who may have limited legal knowledge, financial resources or access to documentation."}]},{"heading":"Legal Aid Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A typical legal-aid matter can involve:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Client Approaches Legal Aid System","Eligibility / Matter Assessment","Initial Legal Interview","Fact & Document Collection","Legal Research","Counsel Assignment / Representation","Court Proceedings","Client Updates","Orders / Further Proceedings","Appeal / Follow-up Where Applicable"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact workflow differs by institution and case type."}]},{"heading":"Client Interviewing Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Legal Aid Counsel must be able to obtain accurate information efficiently."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Client identity"},{"text":"Relevant chronology"},{"text":"Police/court status"},{"text":"Charges or allegations"},{"text":"Important witnesses"},{"text":"Documents"},{"text":"Previous proceedings"},{"text":"Custody status"},{"text":"Immediate legal concerns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Interview framework"},{"type":"flow","items":["What happened?","When did it happen?","Who was involved?","What action has been taken?","What documents exist?","What is the immediate legal issue?","What remedy is available?"]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid making promises about case outcomes."}]},{"heading":"Criminal Legal Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to research:"},{"type":"h","text":"Primary sources"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statutes"},{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Regulations"},{"text":"Court judgments"},{"text":"Constitutional provisions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research questions"},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Is the offence bailable?"},{"text":"What are the applicable procedural requirements?"},{"text":"What is the limitation or filing requirement?"},{"text":"What evidence is legally relevant?"},{"text":"What safeguards apply to the accused?"},{"text":"What remedy is available against an order?"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The ability to locate current primary law is more important than memorizing large numbers of cases."}]},{"heading":"Bail & Remand Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Bail-related work is an important area of criminal practice."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrest procedure"},{"text":"Custody"},{"text":"Remand"},{"text":"Bail principles"},{"text":"Conditions of bail"},{"text":"Default/statutory bail concepts where applicable"},{"text":"Anticipatory bail"},{"text":"Bail cancellation"},{"text":"Appeals/revisions where relevant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Always work from the current procedural law and latest judicial interpretation, because criminal procedure can change."}]},{"heading":"Evidence Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Relevance"},{"text":"Admissibility"},{"text":"Oral evidence"},{"text":"Documentary evidence"},{"text":"Electronic evidence"},{"text":"Expert evidence"},{"text":"Witness examination"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Burden of proof"},{"text":"Presumptions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Modern criminal practice increasingly involves:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CCTV"},{"text":"Mobile-phone records"},{"text":"Digital communications"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Digital photographs"},{"text":"Audio/video evidence"},{"text":"Electronic documents"}]}]},{"heading":"Courtroom Advocacy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"h","text":"Oral Advocacy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Opening submissions"},{"text":"Bail arguments"},{"text":"Objection handling"},{"text":"Examination-in-chief"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Re-examination"},{"text":"Final arguments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Courtroom Discipline"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Court etiquette"},{"text":"File organization"},{"text":"Case preparation"},{"text":"Procedural compliance"},{"text":"Accurate citations"},{"text":"Professional conduct"}]}]},{"heading":"Legal Drafting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Practice drafting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bail applications"},{"text":"Criminal complaints"},{"text":"Applications before courts"},{"text":"Written submissions"},{"text":"Affidavits"},{"text":"Legal notices"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Revision applications"},{"text":"Legal-aid applications"},{"text":"Client representations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"All actual court filings should be prepared and reviewed according to the applicable procedural rules and professional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Human Rights & Access to Justice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Legal Aid Counsel should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Right to legal representation"},{"text":"Due process"},{"text":"Fair trial principles"},{"text":"Rights of persons in custody"},{"text":"Rights of victims"},{"text":"Rights of vulnerable persons"},{"text":"Prisoner rights"},{"text":"Juvenile justice"},{"text":"Gender-based violence"},{"text":"Protection of marginalized communities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role is not simply about winning cases. It is about ensuring that people have meaningful access to the justice system."}]},{"heading":"Legal Aid & Vulnerable Clients","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop communication skills for working with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economically disadvantaged clients"},{"text":"Persons in custody"},{"text":"Children"},{"text":"Women facing violence"},{"text":"Persons with disabilities"},{"text":"Elderly persons"},{"text":"Migrant workers"},{"text":"People with limited legal literacy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Communication should be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["clear","respectful","confidential","non-judgmental."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Legal Aid Clinic Experience","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"During law school, actively participate in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"University legal-aid clinics"},{"text":"Legal-awareness camps"},{"text":"Client counselling"},{"text":"Community legal education"},{"text":"Prison legal-aid initiatives where permitted"},{"text":"NGO legal projects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These experiences help develop practical understanding of access-to-justice problems."}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern criminal-law professional should be comfortable with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Legal Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SCC Online"},{"text":"Manupatra"},{"text":"Indian Kanoon"},{"text":"HeinOnline"},{"text":"Other professional legal databases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Productivity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PDF tools"},{"text":"Google Workspace"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital case files"},{"text":"Case-management systems"},{"text":"Hearing calendars"},{"text":"Document repositories"},{"text":"E-filing workflows where applicable"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Legal Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case-law discovery"},{"text":"Document summarization"},{"text":"Chronology preparation"},{"text":"Contract/document comparison"},{"text":"Legal research organization"},{"text":"Case-file indexing"},{"text":"Drafting first versions of routine documents"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But legal professionals must independently verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statutes"},{"text":"Case citations"},{"text":"Legal propositions"},{"text":"Procedural requirements"},{"text":"Court rules"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Never rely on an unverified AI-generated citation in an actual legal filing."},{"type":"p","text":"Confidential client information should also not be entered into AI systems without appropriate authorization and safeguards."}]},{"heading":"Projects During Law School","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Criminal Case Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze a publicly available judgment:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Facts"},{"text":"Issues"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Arguments"},{"text":"Court reasoning"},{"text":"Final decision"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Bail Research Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare judicial principles relating to bail under current law."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Legal Aid Awareness Program"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a structured legal-literacy project covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal aid"},{"text":"Rights"},{"text":"Available institutions"},{"text":"How to seek assistance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Mock Trial"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a complete simulated criminal trial."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Prison Legal-Aid Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study access-to-justice challenges faced by prisoners using publicly available research and reports."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Early Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Litigation chambers"},{"text":"District courts"},{"text":"Legal NGOs"},{"text":"Legal-aid organizations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Middle Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal-law practices"},{"text":"Trial advocacy"},{"text":"Legal-aid clinics"},{"text":"Human-rights organizations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Seek:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal-law chambers"},{"text":"Legal Services Authorities where internship opportunities are available"},{"text":"Legal-aid organizations"},{"text":"Human-rights organizations"},{"text":"Public-interest legal organizations"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Titles","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Search for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal Law Intern"},{"text":"Litigation Intern"},{"text":"Legal Aid Intern"},{"text":"Legal Research Intern"},{"text":"Human Rights Intern"},{"text":"Trial Advocacy Intern"},{"text":"Public Interest Law Intern"},{"text":"Legal Services Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Employer / Institution Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Environment","Important Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Legal Services Authorities"},{"text":"Legal aid, client handling, court practice"}],[{"text":"Criminal Law Chambers"},{"text":"Trial advocacy, drafting, research"}],[{"text":"District Courts"},{"text":"Procedure, filing, client interaction"}],[{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Human rights, legal awareness"}],[{"text":"Prison Legal-Aid Programs"},{"text":"Criminal procedure, client counselling"}],[{"text":"Human Rights Organizations"},{"text":"Research, advocacy, documentation"}],[{"text":"Law Firms"},{"text":"Research, drafting, litigation"}],[{"text":"Legal Clinics"},{"text":"Client interviewing, legal literacy"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Law"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Evidence law"},{"text":"Trial advocacy"},{"text":"Bail practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human Rights"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human rights law"},{"text":"Prison law"},{"text":"Child rights"},{"text":"Gender justice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advocacy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trial advocacy"},{"text":"Legal drafting"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Client counselling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal research databases"},{"text":"E-filing"},{"text":"Legal technology"},{"text":"Digital evidence fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The most valuable preparation remains actual supervised legal practice and courtroom exposure."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate specializations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LL.M. Criminal Law"},{"text":"LL.M. Criminal & Security Law"},{"text":"LL.M. Human Rights Law"},{"text":"LL.M. Constitutional Law"},{"text":"LL.M. Criminal Justice"},{"text":"LL.M. Public Law"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Research-oriented students can consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal justice research"},{"text":"Human rights research"},{"text":"Penology"},{"text":"Victimology"},{"text":"Constitutional criminal procedure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree is not mandatory to work as an advocate or pursue legal-aid practice."}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Criminal Defence"},{"type":"p","text":"Represent accused persons in criminal proceedings."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Legal Aid"},{"type":"p","text":"Provide representation through recognized legal-aid mechanisms."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Human Rights"},{"type":"p","text":"Work on rights violations and access to justice."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Prison Legal Services"},{"type":"p","text":"Assist prisoners with legal matters."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Juvenile Justice"},{"type":"p","text":"Work on matters involving children in conflict with law or children requiring protection."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Victim Assistance"},{"type":"p","text":"Support victims within the applicable legal framework."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Public Interest Litigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Work on broader access-to-justice and rights issues, subject to professional requirements and the nature of the organization."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Student + Legal Aid Clinic + Internships","2–5 Years"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Junior Advocate / Criminal Law Practice","3–7 Years"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Legal Aid Counsel / Panel Counsel","7–12 Years"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Experienced Legal Aid / Criminal Law Counsel","12+ Years"]},{"type":"p","text":"Senior Counsel / Legal Services Leadership /"},{"type":"p","text":"Human Rights or Access-to-Justice Leadership"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact appointment route and career progression depend on the legal-services authority, state, court, panel requirements and professional experience."}]},{"heading":"Professional Ethics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Legal Aid Counsel must maintain high professional standards."},{"type":"p","text":"Important principles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Conflict-of-interest management"},{"text":"Client dignity"},{"text":"Professional independence"},{"text":"Honest communication"},{"text":"Accurate legal advice"},{"text":"Proper handling of client documents"},{"text":"Avoiding false assurances"},{"text":"Compliance with professional conduct rules"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The lawyer should never guarantee a particular court outcome."}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong law graduate targeting legal-aid work should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understand current criminal law"},{"text":"Research criminal judgments"},{"text":"Analyze evidence"},{"text":"Understand criminal procedure"},{"text":"Draft basic legal documents"},{"text":"Conduct structured client interviews"},{"text":"Understand bail and remand procedures"},{"text":"Present oral arguments in supervised settings"},{"text":"Understand legal-aid mechanisms"},{"text":"Work with vulnerable clients"},{"text":"Maintain confidentiality"},{"text":"Use legal research databases"},{"text":"Understand digital evidence fundamentals"},{"text":"Communicate legal issues clearly"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Portfolio Item","Demonstrates"],"rows":[[{"text":"Criminal Judgment Analysis"},{"text":"Legal research"}],[{"text":"Bail Research Paper"},{"text":"Criminal-law knowledge"}],[{"text":"Mock Trial"},{"text":"Advocacy"}],[{"text":"Legal-Aid Clinic Work"},{"text":"Client interaction"}],[{"text":"Legal Awareness Project"},{"text":"Community engagement"}],[{"text":"Drafting Portfolio"},{"text":"Legal drafting"}],[{"text":"Evidence Analysis"},{"text":"Analytical ability"}],[{"text":"Human Rights Research"},{"text":"Access-to-justice knowledge"}],[{"text":"Legal Research Memo"},{"text":"Professional writing"}],[{"text":"Internship Record"},{"text":"Practical exposure"}]]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Evidence Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Trial Advocacy"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Drafting"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Client Counselling"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Human Rights"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Aid Framework"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Evidence Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Courtroom Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Professional Ethics"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated LLB","Criminal Law Internships","Legal-Aid Clinic","Trial Advocacy + Criminal Procedure","Court Practice","Advocate Qualification/Enrolment","Criminal Law Experience","Legal Aid Panel/Appointment","Legal Aid Counsel","Senior Counsel / Access-to-Justice Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal graduate profile"},{"type":"p","text":"A professionally qualified legal practitioner with strong criminal-law and procedural knowledge, courtroom advocacy, legal drafting, evidence analysis, client counselling, human-rights awareness and practical experience serving individuals who need access to affordable or publicly supported legal representation."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment note","text":"Legal Aid Counsel is not simply an automatic job title obtained after an LLB. In India, court practice requires the applicable professional qualification, enrolment and practice requirements. Appointment to legal-aid panels or positions depends on the relevant NALSA/State Legal Services Authority/District Legal Services Authority framework, current eligibility criteria, experience requirements and panel selection process. Students should verify the latest notification before applying."}]}]}